   "source": [
    "Obviously, the wider the wire gets, the less effective it is to us.\n",
    "\n",
    "In addition, the small difference, originating from different lengths, is most notable at $P=0.3$[W] where, between the shortest and longest wire, the phase shift drops from $\\sim 7$ to $\\sim 6.5$ (looking at $w=1\\mu m$).\n",
    "\n",
    "This is because the total power input is the same but the total heater area is not and 'cause the simulation input power in in units [W/m] where the total power is devided by the area. (source: https://innovationspace.ansys.com/courses/courses/lumerical-heat-materials-and-simulation-objects/lessons/sources-and-monitors-in-ansys-lumerical-heat-lesson-6/)\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, we are better of using a shorter and thinner heater with the same power."
